        <briefdescription>
<para>Creates a grid of positions (Vector3Ds), centered at 0. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>diameter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The shape of the grid is a sphere with this diameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>n_axis_points</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of points used along an axis for the grid. The axis X Y and Z will contain n_axis_points, equispaced. The other regions of space will contain only the points allowed by the size of the sphere.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This function is only available in Python. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
